# Equipping Agents with Agent Skills.map

**Anatomy of a Skill**
Self-contained filesystem directory
SKILL.md (Required)
- YAML frontmatter
  - name (lowercase, max 64 chars)
  - description (routing trigger, max 1024 chars)
- Markdown body with procedural workflows
Optional Subdirectories
- scripts/ for executable Python or Bash utilities
- references/ for deep documentation loaded on demand
- assets/ for templates, schemas, and resources

**Progressive Disclosure**
Prevents context window bloat across large skill libraries
Three-Tier Loading Model
- Tier 1: Discovery
  - Pre-loads only name and description at startup
- Tier 2: Activation
  - Loads full SKILL.md body when prompt matches
- Tier 3: Execution
  - Reads references/ or runs scripts/ just-in-time

**Code Execution & Authoring**
Bridging language reasoning and deterministic code
- Agent runs bundled scripts via shell
- Only script output enters context window
Best Practices
- Start with evaluation tasks to find agent gaps
- Keep SKILL.md concise and split large docs into references/
- Refine naming and descriptions for accurate triggering
- Iterate by reviewing real agent runs

**Security & Auditing [horizontal]**
- Trusted Sources:
  - Estrutura: Only install skills authored or vetted by trusted creators
  - Exemplo: Verified internal repos or official skill registries
- Pre-Use Auditing:
  - Estrutura: Inspect SKILL.md directives, bundled scripts, and dependencies
  - Exemplo: Review network calls, shell commands, and file writes
- Data Boundaries:
  - Estrutura: Restrict external network access when handling sensitive data
  - Exemplo: Sandboxed containers with least-privilege credentials
